  "note": "The connection between speaking scornfully and interpreting for another person remains uncertain. Job 16:20 can be read of either advocacy or mockery. The Arabic verb in Lane at p. 2681 concerns glancing or turning aside, and Akkadian elēṣu in Oracc concerns rejoicing. Neither establishes the sense or older consonant of the Hebrew. The productive key l.bn.aa counts both verbs and nominal scoffers."
